{#- Run-wide execution record, rendered once after the last
    transcript: which requested scanners ran, errored, or never
    executed. Per-label coverage lives in each transcript's
    reliability audit; this block only accounts for execution. A
    scanner executes once per stored transcript (each epoch is its
    own transcript), so the denominator is transcripts. -#}
<section id="scan-status" class="section"><h3>Scan execution &amp; coverage</h3>
<p class="meta explainer">Run-wide record for the stored scan (all epochs): <strong>execution {{ scan_status_view.execution }}</strong>. Execution completion does not establish usable labels; per-label coverage is in the <a href="#reliability-audit">reliability audit</a>.</p>
<div class="relmap-scroll"><table class="relmap">
<tr><th>scanner</th><th>transcripts scanned</th><th>errors</th></tr>
{% for row in scan_status_view.rows %}<tr><th>{{ row.name }}{% if row.sub %}<br/><span class="relmap-sub">{{ row.sub }}</span>{% endif %}</th>{% for cell in (row.scanned, row.errors) %}<td{% if cell.bg %} style="background:{{ cell.bg }};color:{{ cell.fg }}"{% endif %}>{{ cell.text }}</td>{% endfor %}</tr>
{% endfor %}</table></div>
{% if scan_status_view.unmounted %}
<p class="meta">{{ scan_status_view.unmounted|join(", ") }}: stored results with no mounted report layer, so no section of this report renders them; pass the matching Layer via extra_layers to include them.</p>
{% endif %}
{% if scan_status_view.errors %}
<details class="event event-list"><summary>{{ scan_status_view.errors|length }} recorded analysis error(s)</summary><ol>{% for error in scan_status_view.errors %}<li>{{ error.scanner }}{% if error.transcript_id %} · transcript {{ error.transcript_id }}{% endif %} · {{ error.message }}</li>{% endfor %}</ol></details>
{% endif %}
</section>
